            "text": "{\n  \"judgments\": [\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0000\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F004\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"In draft C0002, the actor was incorrectly assigned to the employer. Under subsection (e)(2) and paragraph (B), the duty to provide notice is placed on the employee ('the employee— ... (B) shall provide the employer with not less than 30 days’ notice'). Correcting the actor and actor_quote to 'the employee' is necessary and faithful to the source.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0001\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F004\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"Under subsection (e)(2)(B), the duty to provide advance notice of leave to the employer belongs to the employee, not the health care provider. Changing the actor to 'the health care provider' is factually incorrect.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0002\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F004\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The exception in paragraph (B) ('except that if the date of the treatment requires leave to begin in less than 30 days, the employee shall provide such notice as is practicable') directly qualifies the 30-day advance notice requirement in C0002. Linking C0004 to qualify C0002 with relation 'exception' accurately repairs the missing qualification link.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"supported\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"proposal_id\": \"P0003\",\n      \"source_refs\": [\"F004\", \"F005\", \"F006\"],\n      \"rationale\": \"The exception in paragraph (B) governs the timing of the notice requirement (C0002). It does not qualify the duty under paragraph (A) (C0001) to make reasonable efforts to schedule medical treatment so as not to unduly disrupt operations. Linking C0004 to C0001 is incorrect.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"unsupported\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
